  [36mTIP [39m [1mB7[22m Vary includes Accept, so CDNs cache the two formats separately  [38;2;210;104;94m█[39m[38;2;213;108;98m█[39m[38;2;216;112;102m█[39m[38;2;219;116;106m█[39m[38;2;92;92;86m░░░░[39m [33m2 of 4[39m
      Vary does not include Accept on the HTML response. A CDN can cache that
      side's response and serve it to a visitor asking for the other format.
      [90mHTML Vary: "rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch,[39m
      [90mnext-router-segment-prefetch, Accept-Encoding"; markdown Vary: "Accept,[39m
      [90mAccept-Encoding".[39m
      [38;2;90;162;208m→ Add `Vary: Accept` to the HTML response. Some frameworks will not let[39m
      [38;2;90;162;208m  middleware set it on a response they created; a CDN or reverse-proxy[39m
      [38;2;90;162;208m  rule in front of the app is the way through.[39m

